  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Prolonged stretch of dry weather across southern New \nEngland. Moderating afternoon temperatures this weekend, though \nchilly mornings will bring widespread frost away from the immediate \ncoast.\n\nStrong high pressure continues to sit over southern New England. \nGood radiational cooling overnight with widespread frost can be \nexpected tonight and Sunday night. Lows tonight may fall well into \nthe 20s in the higher elevations of the interior tonight along with \nother spots that radiate quite well. Closer to the coasts and \ntowards Worcester, expect lows in the 40s and upper 30s. 925 mb \ntemperatures improve to around 10C overnight and continue Monday, \nthen to around 12C overnight Monday. Lows Sunday night won't be\nas low as tonight's as a result, but expect temperatures to\nstill fall into the upper 20s in the interior and generally\nsettle around freezing in areas that radiate out well, with 40s\nand upper 30s still expected in coastal areas. Highs Monday \nwill improve to the mid to upper 60s and clear skies are \nexpected to continue.\n\nA prolonged stretch of dry but pleasant autumn weather is in store \nfor Southern New England that continues into a large portion of\nthe upcoming workweek. Expansive area of surface high pressure \nof around 1030-1034 mb will remain anchored across the Northeast\nand mid- Atlantic region, with mild days and cool nights with \nstrong diurnal temperature ranges. About the only nuanced \ndifference is that a cold front sags southward Monday night into\nTuesday with a cooler northern-stream airmass filtering \nsouthward; but the front is moisture-starved and only seems \ncapable of producing some enhanced cloudiness Monday evening and\na cooldown in high temps moving into next week. Mildest days \nlook to be this weekend with temperatures in the mid to upper \n60s, but there could be a shot at 70 degrees with several days \nof dry weather serving as a mild feedback mechanism for \noverachieving maximum temps over guidance. Highs then cool off \ninto the mid 50s to low 60s for early next week as the cooler \nlower-level airmass works it way in (925 mb temps dip to around \n+2 to +4C), only modifying toward mid to late next week.",
